xnu 0294: build the kernel with an upstream clang and no Apple SDK

Upstream clang has none of the XNU signature builtins: every kalloc_type view
turns into a data view, kalloc_type_view_copy() keeps none of them, and the
iterator's assert then panics in kernel_bootstrap before the ring is armed.
The builtins fall back to a data-only summary and both iterators return when
there is no view to sort, which keeps kalloc_type() working without the
type-metadata fast paths.

The Linux iig emits the declarations but not every DriverKit definition, so
the kernel links `IOUserClient::CreateActionKernelCompletion` from the tree
instead of the generated file. `XNU_SKIP_SYMBOLSETS=1` skips the kext symbol
sets, which this kernel-only build never links. XCRUN/PAX/PLUTIL/codesign come
from PATH. The crypto assembly uses the vN.4s syntax with upstream clang too,
because the qN form is Apple's assembler syntax. The profiling runtime and
__cxa_atexit get link shims.

